<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Hardened-runtime exceptions for the Mio shell. These three are what
      electron-builder applies by default; checking them in makes the set a
      decision rather than an upstream default that can shift under us.

      allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        V8. Required by Electron itself and by the dsh runtime child, which is
        the same binary re-entered with ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.

      disable-library-validation
        The runtime child loads native modules that are not signed by this
        team: koffi (FFI), sharp/libvips, node-pty, @vscode/ripgrep, and
        node-addon-require-builtin. electron-builder re-signs them with our
        Developer ID during packaging, but the child resolves them from
        app.asar.unpacked at runtime and library validation would still reject
        anything it decides is foreign. This is the entitlement doing real work
        here — the archived desktop app had two native modules, this shell has
        thirteen.

      Deliberately NOT carried over from the archived app
      (archive/packages/desktop/resources/entitlements.plist):

      - com.apple.security.cs.disable-executable-page-protection
        A blunt instrument, and nothing here needs it: the packaged app runs
        with hardened runtime today and boots the runtime, loads every native
        module, and serves the UI.
      - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
        The shell sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, which is read by Electron, not by
        dyld. No DYLD_* variable is set anywhere in packages/shell.
      - com.apple.security.device.audio-input
        For dictation, which is Phase 3 (MIGRATION.md). Add it back together
        with NSMicrophoneUsageDescription when the ASR plugin lands — an
        entitlement for a capability the app does not have is a review flag.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
